&lt;h2 id="about-the-speaker" class="relative group"&gt;About the speaker &lt;span class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100"&gt;&lt;a class="group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700" style="text-decoration-line: none !important;" href="#about-the-speaker" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;João Thallis is self-taught. He decided to learn programming as a teenager to create games, and learned Elixir to complete a technical challenge for a position at Stone Pagamentos, then the country&amp;rsquo;s fifth-largest acquiring company. After a two-year internship at Stone, he was a software developer at Conta Stone, a digital payments account built with Elixir, his favorite programming language.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>